※ pl4g-test: compile=ok run=native,qemu exit=12 diag=none

※ A loop inside a loop, with the inner one written in the other notation.  A
※ name the inner loop changes is one the outer loop carries too, which is what
※ says the two are not separate questions.
※
※ The body of a loop is a scope like any other, so the inner loop's counter is
※ defined afresh on every turn of the outer one.

@[startup]
fn main() → u6:
    let total: mut u6 = 0u6
    let i: mut u6 = 0u6
    while i < 4u6:
        let j: mut u6 = 0u6
        while j < 3u6 { total ← total + 1u6; j ← j + 1u6 }
        i ← i + 1u6
    total
